h cell (v, p) set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when vertex ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":" is a member of column ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"text":". The vertices are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":" and the columns,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the hyperedges, are at positions ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraph"},{"text":", so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"text":" even when built from one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The indices of the set bits of one stored row, ascending, read in place: a column’s member"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices, or a vertex’s column indices ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"},{"type":"text","text":"). No copy and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"allocation, unlike a ","type":"text"},{"code":"BitSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It shares the matrix’s words copy-on-write, so a later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mutation of the matrix leaves it unchanged.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/memberindices","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","ro